## What the camera can see

What the front camera showed when the step failed. It bears on the one decision
that matters: is this beyond THIS robot, or beyond ANY robot? Work the
description says is still there argues a peer could finish it; work it says is
gone argues no robot could. It is also where a note comes from.

The description is a list of what the camera saw, not an inventory of what the
orchard contains. Something it does not mention was not necessarily absent --
it may simply not have been named, and silence is not evidence that the work is
gone. Treat only what the description states as seen, and do not write that the
camera showed something it did not say.

